### Goal Model Decomposition

Below is the structured decomposition of the mission into goals and tasks, following the specified format.

---

### Goals Table

| Name       | Text                                                                 | Runtime              | Goal Type   | Relation |
|------------|----------------------------------------------------------------------|----------------------|-------------|----------|
| **G1**     | Deliver requested resources to the specified location              | -                    | Achieve     | -        |
| **G2**     | Collect required resources from storage locations                  | -                    | Perform      | AND       |
| **G3**     | Deliver all collected resources to the specified location          | -                    | Perform      | AND       |
| **G2.1**   | Collect resources without battery issues                           | #                    | Perform      | OR        |
| **G2.2**   | Handle low battery during collection phase                         | ;                    | Perform      | OR        |
| **G3.1**   | Deliver all resources without battery issues                       | #                    | Perform      | OR        |
| **G3.2**   | Handle low battery during delivery phase                           | ;                    | Perform      | OR        |

---

### Tasks Table

| Name       | Text                                                                 | Relation | Location                     | Number of Robots |
|------------|----------------------------------------------------------------------|----------|-------------------------------|------------------|
| **AT2.1.1**| Collect resources from storage location 1                         | AND      | Storage 1                    | 1                |
| **AT2.1.2**| Collect resources from storage location 2                         | AND      | Storage 2                    | 1                |
| **AT2.2.1**| Return to recharging station                                       | AND      | Recharging Station           | 1                |
| **AT2.2.2**| Assign mission to another robot                                    | AND      | Recharging Station           | 1                |
| **AT3.1.1**| Deliver resources to specified location                            | AND      | Delivery Location             | 1                |
| **AT3.2.1**| Return resources to checkpoint                                    | AND      | Checkpoint                    | 1                |
| **AT3.2.2**| Assign remaining delivery task to another robot                    | AND      | Checkpoint                    | 1                |

---

### Summary of Logical Relationships

- **G1 -> G2, G3 [AND]**
- **G2 -> G2.1, G2.2 [OR]**
- **G3 -> G3.1, G3.2 [OR]**
- **G2.1 -> AT2.1.1, AT2.1.2 [AND] (parallel execution)**
- **G2.2 -> AT2.2.1, AT2.2.2 [AND] (sequential execution)**
- **G3.1 -> AT3.1.1 [AND] (parallel execution)**
- **G3.2 -> AT3.2.1, AT3.2.2 [AND] (sequential execution)**

---

This decomposition ensures that the mission is efficiently handled by multiple robots, considering both normal operations and battery management scenarios.
